Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — individual review draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: Individual scene draft; whole-film pass provisionally accepted, individual author review pending

INT. CITY CAFÉ - DAY

Elias and Zoe sit with exits in view. Voss and Vale arrive separately. The public room constrains everyone, including their choices about force.

Voss shows Mac's recovery terms. Vale admits that the delegated paperwork survived casual checks but they did not independently confirm the supposed guardian's authority. They warn a replacement team may come. Elias wants names and routes; Zoe wants to know why Mac called her property.

Vale suggests taking Zoe aside while adults settle an exit. Zoe stays seated.

ZOE
People keep calling it a safe handover when the person being handed over can't say no.

Voss withdraws the proposal. The men are not yet allies. Then Zoe notices a watcher beyond the café's own coverage. Someone used a route the contractors thought isolated.
